  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">START Fund ALERT 908 Uganda (Anticipation of Ebola outbreak)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This response initiative aims to reduce the risk of Ebola transmission within and beyond Kampala and Mbale districts. All implementing agencies are actively participating in UN coordination meetings, ensuring awareness and responsiveness. Key actions will commence within 7 days, guided by a rapid needs assessment and close coordination with the Ministry of Health (MoH) and partners, while leveraging existing structures and local resources as outlined in the national response plan. Key interventions to include inclusive community-based information dissemination including hygiene promotion, strengthening access to WASH facilities, strengthening health safety protocols for frontliners and providing them trainings on Psychological First Aid.</narrative>
  </description>
